以及它将如何改变
the work, how it's going to change.

1183
01:01:51,910 --> 01:01:55,730
到目前为止 我听到的是 工作中会有更多在审阅别人产出的内容
What I'm hearing so far is there's gonna be a lot more reviewing of other people's output

1184
01:01:55,730 --> 01:01:56,370
这会成为工作的一部分
as a part of the work.

1185
01:01:57,150 --> 01:02:00,870
其次 会有大量近乎是照看AI智能体的工作 让它们
And then two, there's gonna be a lot of like almost babysitting of AI agents to make them

1186
01:02:00,870 --> 01:02:05,610
在部署时按你想要的方式去做事 然后在过程中不断给它们修修剪剪
do the thing you want them to do for deploying and then just gardening them along the way,

1187
01:02:05,650 --> 01:02:06,930
确保它们持续把工作做好
make sure they continue to do their work.

1188
01:02:08,650 --> 01:02:11,130
在我们进入第三个话题之前 还有别的吗
Anything else before we get into our third bucket?

1189
01:02:11,330 --> 01:02:19,410
我会把它理解成 与其说是照看智能体 不如说是你的前线团队
I would sort of split it into less babysitting agents and more your forward deployed team

1190
01:02:19,410 --> 01:02:24,590
在努力构建一个完整系统 让那些知识储备较少的人也能用这个系统
is trying to build a whole system that makes it so that people who have less knowledge can

1191
01:02:24,590 --> 01:02:27,850
而不会做出什么蠢事
use that system without like doing something dumb.

1192
01:02:28,250 --> 01:02:31,750
而这本身就是一个非常有趣的工程挑战
And that's like a really interesting engineering challenge.

1193
01:02:32,150 --> 01:02:34,810
我觉得用“照看”这个词会让人感觉
I think babysitting kind of makes it feel like it's,

1194
01:02:35,670 --> 01:02:36,610
是啊 你好像只是
yeah, you're just kind of like,

1195
01:02:36,610 --> 01:02:38,710
在那儿等它出错 然后再去修修补补之类的
waiting for it to fuck up and then fixing it or whatever.

1196
01:02:39,390 --> 01:02:41,410
也有可能是那样
And that can be the case.

1197
01:02:41,470 --> 01:02:45,670
但我觉得很大一部分其实是一个极其有趣的工程挑战，也就是要构建一个
But I think a lot of it is this extremely interesting engineering challenge of building a

1198
01:02:45,670 --> 01:02:50,510
系统，让组织里其他所有人都能做过去只有技术岗位才能做的事情
system to enable everybody else in your organization to do what used to be a technical job.

1199
01:02:50,970 --> 01:02:52,370
然后如果你不是那类人
And then if you're not one of those people,

1200
01:02:52,530 --> 01:02:53,890
比如你是数据科学家之类的
like you're the data scientist or whatever,

1201
01:02:54,010 --> 01:02:58,090
你就可以借助AI在那些非常重要的问题上挖得更深 而这些问题最终
you can go a lot deeper with AI into like really important questions that eventually

1202
01:02:58,090 --> 01:03:02,850
很可能会渗透到前线工程团队正在做的工作里
probably filter into the work that the forward deployed engineering team is doing,

1203
01:03:03,290 --> 01:03:08,470
但它们更具生成性 更新颖 而且你在处理的是更难的问题
but is like more generative and more new and you're dealing with harder questions.

1204
01:03:09,050 --> 01:03:14,710
还有最后一件我觉得非常有趣的事 是我认为我们会读到更多
One last thing that I think is really interesting is I think that we will be reading way

1205
01:03:14,710 --> 01:03:17,650
文档和邮件里的AI生成文字
more AI generated writing in documents and emails,

1206
01:03:17,990 --> 01:03:19,230
而且我们会喜欢这样
and we will like it.

1207
01:03:19,970 --> 01:03:25,770
而且在编程里我们其实已经在这么做了 比如阅读由AI写的方案文档
And I think we are already doing this in coding where we read plan documents.

1208
01:03:26,470 --> 01:03:29,670
我并不希望工程师手写一份方案文档
Like I don't want an engineer to hand write a plan document.

1209
01:03:29,730 --> 01:03:30,710
那会非常傻
That would be very silly.

1210
01:03:31,050 --> 01:03:32,550
显而易见地傻
It would be obviously silly.

1211
01:03:34,830 --> 01:03:35,990
我觉得在别的地方也是一样
And I think the same is true,

1212
01:03:36,090 --> 01:03:41,190
比如在2025年底我们做季度规划的时候
you know, when we did our quarterly planning at the end of 2025,

1213
01:03:41,670 --> 01:03:43,790
我们完全是用notion智能体来做的
we did it all with notion agents.

1214
01:03:44,250 --> 01:03:47,850
我们名义上有一堆notion智能体 但本质上就是一个notion智能体
And we just had a bunch of notion agents and we had really one notion agent.

1215
01:03:48,010 --> 01:03:50,530
然后我们有一份公司顶层战略
And then we had a top level company strategy.

1216
01:03:51,650 --> 01:03:59,330
接着我们让公司里所有人都去和这个智能体对话 由它来问他们
And then we had everybody in the company just talked to an agent and it asked them about

1217
01:03:59,330 --> 01:04:00,390
去年发生了什么
what happened last year.

1218
01:04:00,810 --> 01:04:01,470
进展如何
How did it go?

1219
01:04:01,570 --> 01:04:02,210
你的目标是什么
What were your goals?

1220
01:04:02,450 --> 01:04:03,870
你今年想做什么
What do you want to do this year?

1221
01:04:04,130 --> 01:04:04,930
你的指标是什么
What are your metrics?

1222
01:04:05,070 --> 01:04:06,270
它会提出反问 然后会继续问
It pushed back. And then it was like,

1223
01:04:06,310 --> 01:04:08,550
这和公司的整体理念有什么关系
how does this relate to the overall company idea?

1224
01:04:08,690 --> 01:04:09,690
类似这一整套问题
Like all that kind of stuff.

1225
01:04:09,850 --> 01:04:13,830
然后我就拿到了一堆质量极高的AI生成的
And then I got these like incredibly good AI generated,

1226
01:04:14,030 --> 01:04:19,770
比如每个团队各个部分的战略报告或季度计划
like strategy reports or quarterly plans for each part of each team.

1227
01:04:19,910 --> 01:04:20,990
接着我就可以进去看 然后想
And then I could go in and be like,

1228
01:04:21,430 --> 01:04:24,590
好 哪些人需要互相沟通
okay, who needs to talk to each other?

1229
01:04:24,690 --> 01:04:27,470
哪些团队其实需要互相沟通 但他们自己还没意识到
Like which teams need to talk to each other that like don't know they need to talk to each other?

1230
01:04:29,590 --> 01:04:35,490
还有 比如哪些计划其实质量很低 哪些又是高质量的
And, you know, which one of these is like actually low quality or which one of these is high quality?

1231
01:04:35,590 --> 01:04:36,430
类似这一整套判断
Like all that kind of stuff.

1232
01:04:36,550 --> 01:04:37,890
这让整个信息处理过程轻松了很多
It makes it a lot easier to process.

1233
01:04:39,010 --> 01:04:40,430
而现在我一直都在看到这种情况
And I see that all the time now.

1234
01:04:40,570 --> 01:04:44,330
我持续不断地在收到AI生成的内容
Like I consistently get AI generated stuff.

1235
01:04:44,590 --> 01:04:48,370
而且粗制滥造的AI文档和不是粗制滥造的AI文档之间是有区别的
And there's a difference between an AI generated document that's slop and not.

1236
01:04:48,990 --> 01:04:55,090
粗制滥造的那种 就是他们花在生成上的时间比我阅读所花的时间还少
And the slop one is it took them less time to make it than it takes me to read it.

1237
01:04:56,010 --> 01:04:57,930
而且他们并不对文档里的每一句话负责
And they don't stand behind every line.

1238
01:04:59,050 --> 01:05:02,010
所以我的预期是 如果你给我发一份AI生成的文档
So my expectation is if you send me an AI generated document,

1239
01:05:02,090 --> 01:05:02,870
我觉得那很好
I think that's great.

1240
01:05:03,310 --> 01:05:07,790
但如果我们讨论的时候一看就知道你根本不知道里面写了什么 那就是大忌
And if we talk about it and it's clear you have no idea what's in it, like big no-no.

1241
01:05:08,230 --> 01:05:08,970
这种事是不允许的
Not allowed to do that.

1242
01:05:10,130 --> 01:05:16,450
我认为我们现在对AI生成内容的这种排斥感会逐渐消失
And I think we have this aversion to AI generated stuff that will go away.

1243
01:05:16,590 --> 01:05:21,630
因为在我团队里有人很好地给GPT-4.1下指令时 它能写出的那种战略文档
Because the kind of strategy document that GPT-4.1 can write when it's directed well by

1244
01:05:21,630 --> 01:05:27,430
远远好过他们自己在键盘上东敲西敲
someone on my team is way better than like them just like dinking and dunking like their

1245
01:05:27,430 --> 01:05:28,350
靠手指慢慢敲出来的东西
fingers on the keyboard.

1246
01:05:28,590 --> 01:05:30,030
是啊 因为大多数人写得真的很糟
Right. Like most people are really bad.

1247
01:05:31,530 --> 01:05:32,730
门槛非常低
The bar is low.

1248
01:05:33,130 --> 01:05:36,010
对 邮件也是一样
Yeah. And same thing with email.

1249
01:05:36,190 --> 01:05:39,270
现在我大部分邮件都是由GPT-4.1和Codex写的
Like most of my email is written by GPT-4.1 and Codex right now.

1250
01:05:39,590 --> 01:05:46,710
说实话 我甚至更希望邮件上直接标明是GPT-4.1写的 我可能会改成那样
And I honestly would prefer it to say that it's coming from GPT-4.1 and I may change it to do that.

1251
01:05:47,350 --> 01:05:54,810
但前几天我有个经历 是我要给我们的一位
But I had this experience the other day where I had to send an email to one of our

1252
01:05:54,810 --> 01:05:59,250
投资人发邮件 然后我让Codex去写
investors and I asked Codex to go do it.

1253
01:05:59,490 --> 01:06:02,550
按理说Codex知道要先来问我 通常它也会这么做
And Codex knows to ask me and it usually does.

1254
01:06:02,690 --> 01:06:04,590
但这次它没有
But this time it didn't.

1255
01:06:05,470 --> 01:06:08,610
它直接把邮件发出去了 而我完全没看
It just sent the email and I didn't look at it at all.

1256
01:06:09,050 --> 01:06:09,830
当时我心想 糟糕
And I was like, fuck.

1257
01:06:10,050 --> 01:06:12,670
所以我赶紧去发件箱里看了一眼 然后我发现
And so I went to my sent and looked at it and I was like,

1258
01:06:12,730 --> 01:06:13,910
哦 这完全就是我自己会发的那种邮件
oh, this is exactly what I would send.

1259
01:06:14,110 --> 01:06:18,750
所以很多时候 它已经非常接近我的风格了
And so it's like it's pretty close to to that a lot of the time.

1260
01:06:19,090 --> 01:06:20,670
可能就是稍微有点太正式
It can be like a little over formal.

1261
01:06:20,870 --> 01:06:24,810
还有几件事 就是当你认真想一想
And there's a couple of things that that it's just when you really think about it,

1262
01:06:24,810 --> 01:06:30,890
你会发现你大部分邮件其实都挺机械化
most of your email is kind of it's not it's kind of rote.

1263
01:06:31,130 --> 01:06:32,230
有点平淡无奇
It's kind of prosaic.

1264
01:06:32,310 --> 01:06:37,350
我当然希望由我自己来思考邮件应该表达什么
It's kind of I definitely want to be the one to think about what it should say,

1265
01:06:37,570 --> 01:06:38,870
就是它到底应该说什么
like what what it should say.

1266
01:06:38,970 --> 01:06:42,290
但具体的句子怎么写 对我来说没那么重要
But the actual sentences don't matter that much to me.

1267
01:06:42,290 --> 01:06:44,050
通常如此 偶尔在某些情况下就非常重要
Usually, sometimes they do a lot.

1268
01:06:44,170 --> 01:06:44,990
而我是一个写作者
And this is coming from a writer.

1269
01:06:45,290 --> 01:06:46,970
我非常在乎写作
Like I care a ton about writing.

1270
01:06:47,130 --> 01:06:49,610
我认为人类写作极其重要
I think that human writing is incredibly important.

1271
01:06:50,350 --> 01:06:52,670
而且我本来以为我们只会发表人类写作
And I expect we only publish human writing.

1272
01:06:52,850 --> 01:06:54,690
实际上 我们发表的是人类写作和AI写作的混合
Actually, we publish a mix of human and AI writing,

1273
01:06:54,770 --> 01:06:55,690
但我们总是会标注清楚
but we always label it.

1274
01:06:56,150 --> 01:06:58,970
有时候在某些内容上有一个AI合著者是件挺好的事
Sometimes it's nice to have an AI co-author on certain things.

1275
01:06:59,590 --> 01:07:02,590
我绝对认为人类写作是重要的
I absolutely think that human writing is important.

1276
01:07:02,890 --> 01:07:10,010
而且我觉得人们对AI写作的那种本能反感其实挺可笑的
And I think that the the the reaction or the aversion to AI writing is silly.

1277
01:07:10,010 --> 01:07:12,490
这是一个非常有趣的视角
It's such an interesting lens on that.

1278
01:07:12,930 --> 01:07:14,730
因为当人们想到AI写作时
Because when people think about AI writing,

1279
01:07:14,950 --> 01:07:17,330
我会想到的是社交媒体和视频
I think about social media and videos.

1280
01:07:17,950 --> 01:07:18,970
而你的观点是 在公司内部
And your point is internally,

1281
01:07:19,130 --> 01:07:22,450
如果你只是做规划 文档 邮件之类的工作
if you're just like working on planning and documents and email and things like that,

1282
01:07:22,530 --> 01:07:25,450
那就没那么可怕 按你说的
like that is much less scary that it's AI written in your to your point,

1283
01:07:25,590 --> 01:07:26,510
人们其实已经在这么做了
people are already doing this.

1284
01:07:26,830 --> 01:07:29,990
很多时候你甚至更愿意它是AI写的 因为反正人类在这些事情上做得也很差
You almost prefer it a lot of times because people are really bad at doing this anyway.

1285
01:07:30,250 --> 01:07:31,590
在对外内容上我们也是这么做的
We have this too for external stuff.

1286
01:07:31,650 --> 01:07:32,950
比如我们会发布各种指南
Like we publish all these guides,

1287
01:07:33,290 --> 01:07:36,730
而这些指南都是由智能体辅助完成的
and the guides are agent-assisted.

1288
01:07:37,030 --> 01:07:38,150
智能体是合著者之一
And the agent is a co-author.

1289
01:07:39,170 --> 01:07:41,990
而且这些内容本来就是既给人看 也给智能体看
And they're intended to be read both by humans and by agents.

1290
01:07:42,450 --> 01:07:45,990
这是因为当你在写一大堆信息性内容时
And that's because if you're writing a huge informational thing,

1291
01:07:46,010 --> 01:07:46,950
你其实一直都在做这种事
I mean, you do this all the time.

1292
01:07:49,790 --> 01:07:51,510
为了真正把这些内容用起来
In order to really apply it,

1293
01:07:51,550 --> 01:07:53,990
最好的方式就是让你的智能体把它们全部读进去
the best way to do that is just have your agent ingest it.

1294
01:07:55,230 --> 01:08:00,870
然后记住 下次我在做定价时 提醒我这份指南 我们再一起
And remember the next time I'm doing pricing to remind me of this guide and we'll go

1295
01:08:00,870 --> 01:08:02,050
把它过一遍 或者做类似的事情
through it together or whatever.

1296
01:08:02,690 --> 01:08:07,450
它能让你把这些想法落实到执行层面上好得多
It allows you to operationalize the ideas much better.

1297
01:08:07,650 --> 01:08:11,690
而且它还能让你挖掘得更深入，因为智能体可以在一秒钟内读完大约一万页
And it allows you to go much deeper because agents can read like 10,000 pages in like a second.

1298
01:08:12,630 --> 01:08:16,890
所以你可以和人类只聊故事、本质问题和核心想法
And so you can you talk to the human about the story and the stuff that matters and the core ideas.

1299
01:08:17,030 --> 01:08:20,230
而智能体掌握了所有细节，在你需要时可以替你调用
And the agent has all the details that it can then apply for you when you need it.

1300
01:08:20,710 --> 01:08:21,110
太棒了
Awesome.

1301
01:08:22,110 --> 01:08:25,650
在进入最后一个类别之前，这一类还有别的要补充的吗
Anything else in this category before we get into our final category?

1302
01:08:26,070 --> 01:08:27,950
没有 好 那我们开始吧
No. Okay, let's do it.

1303
01:08:28,350 --> 01:08:33,610
最后一类就是 在我们正走向的这个AI未来里 谁会取得成功
So the final bucket is just who will be successful in this AI future that we are

1304
01:08:33,610 --> 01:08:39,190
以及在接下来一两年里 人们该做些什么才能获得成功
approaching slash what should people be working on to be successful in this next year or two?

1305
01:08:39,610 --> 01:08:43,910
我对产品经理超级超级看好
I am super, super bullish on PMs.

1306
01:08:45,250 --> 01:08:47,750
而且我知道你的听众大概会很喜欢听到这个
And I know that your audience will probably love that.

1307
01:08:48,830 --> 01:08:56,690
但让我深信这一点的一个个人案例是我们内部有这么一个人，他叫马库斯
But my anecdotal case that has convinced me of this is we have this guy internally, and his name is Marcus.

1308
01:08:57,290 --> 01:08:59,810
他负责Spiral 也就是我们的写作应用
And he runs Spiral, which is our writing app.

1309
01:09:01,530 --> 01:09:03,690
Marcus本职是个产品经理
Marcus is a PM by training.

1310
01:09:04,750 --> 01:09:08,530
之前他负责Axios
He previously ran Axios,

1311
01:09:08,530 --> 01:09:10,070
Axios的写作产品
Axios is writing product.

1312
01:09:10,570 --> 01:09:13,350
他当时是产品经理 带着一个大团队 把那个产品做到了
And was it was a PM and had a big team and it got to,

1313
01:09:13,530 --> 01:09:16,050
你知道 年经常性收入几千万美元的规模
you know, tens of millions in of revenue in ARR.

1314
01:09:16,990 --> 01:09:20,630
后来他从那份工作上休息了一年
And he took a year off that job,

1315
01:09:20,710 --> 01:09:22,430
然后整个人变成了深度AI信仰者
and just got super AI pilled,

1316
01:09:22,670 --> 01:09:25,890
花时间把Cursor用得非常溜
and just learned how to use cursor basically really well.

1317
01:09:26,130 --> 01:09:27,090
现在我觉得他在用Claude Code
Now, I think he uses Claude Code,

1318
01:09:27,190 --> 01:09:29,290
但有很长一段时间他是超级Cursor信徒
but he was extremely cursor pilled for a long time.

1319
01:09:30,490 --> 01:09:33,470
我会说 他算是“轻度技术型”
And he's, I would call him like lightly technical.

1320
01:09:35,560 --> 01:09:37,360
比如知道什么是数据库迁移
Like knows what a database migration is,

1321
01:09:37,380 --> 01:09:38,620
如果必须看代码
like, if he has to look at the code,

1322
01:09:38,680 --> 01:09:40,020
我觉得他也能看懂
I think he can understand it.

1323
01:09:40,060 --> 01:09:43,660
但问题是 一年前我们根本不可能雇他来干现在这份工作
But he's like, I we never could have hired him to do this job,

1324
01:09:43,920 --> 01:09:45,060
就连一年前都不行
